        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3a8431b1-850d-51c3-ba7f-ac1ea44153eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: West Texas, High Plains, Trans-Pecos, Western High Plains, Llano Estacado\n- Products: Buda Limestone, Woodbine Formation, Maness Shale, Eagle Ford Group, Austin Chalk\n- Concepts: geological formations, Late Cretaceous, stratigraphy\n\nFacts:\n- The Buda Limestone is a geological formation in the High Plains and Trans-Pecos regions of West Texas, and its strata date to the Late Cretaceous.\n- The southern region of the Western High Plains ecology region contains the geological formation known as Llano Estacado.\n- Llano Estacado can be seen from a short distance or on satellite maps.\n- The Woodbine Formation overlies the Maness Shale, the Buda Limestone, or older rocks.\n- The Woodbine Formation underlies the Eagle Ford Group or Austin Chalk.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
